{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Kats2016-Ge10nm-on-Au",
  "Source": "M. A. Kats and F. Capasso, \"Optical absorbers based on strong interference in ultra-thin films,\" Laser Photonics Rev., 1-15 (2016) (Early View; volume and final pages not printed in this copy). doi:10.1002/lpor.201600098 - Sec. 6, p. 5 and Fig. 3: 10 nm a-Ge on Au, reflectance minimum at lambda0 ~ 530 nm where a-Ge n ~ 4.3 + 2.1i",
  "Notes": "Ultra-thin amorphous Ge film on an opaque gold substrate: reflectance minimum (strong absorption) in the visible for a film far thinner than a quarter wave\nSpecification: Reflectance minimum / absorption maximum near 530 nm at normal incidence.\nReported: Reflectance minimum at lambda0 ~ 530 nm for the 10 nm Ge film (p. 5); the reflection phase phi21 ~ 11 deg and 2*phi21 corresponds to propagation through ~7.5 nm of film. Fig. 3(b) (measured, normal incidence) shows the 10 nm film minimum R roughly 0.2 near 520-550 nm (read off the plot, approximate); Fig. 3(c): 70-80 % of incident light absorbed in the Ge for 10-15 nm films.\nNotes: Ge index is given only at one wavelength (the measured dispersion of Fig. 3(a) is plotted, not tabulated), so this design is meaningful only at 530 nm; do not evaluate a spectrum with the constant. Au optical constants are not given (Fig. 3(a) measured, plotted only); the library 'Au' will differ somewhat from the paper's evaporated film. Au is optically thick (opaque) and treated as the substrate. Other Ge thicknesses in Fig. 3 (7, 15, 20, 25 nm) are not rebuilt because their minima lie away from 530 nm where no index is printed.\nLayers from Sec. 6, p. 5 and Fig. 3: 10 nm a-Ge on Au, reflectance minimum at lambda0 ~ 530 nm where a-Ge n ~ 4.3 + 2.1i; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), compare with the paper: ours R 18.2 % at 530 nm (the Ge index holds only there; Au Johnson & Christy); paper R minimum near 530 nm, measured ~0.2. The a-Ge index is the paper’s value at 530 nm only, so only that wavelength means anything; Au is Johnson & Christy.",
  "Wavelength": [
    530
  ],
